          "title": "sollen: should",
          "body": "**sollen** = should, to be supposed to. Use it for what someone else says you should do: the doctor, your mother, your boss.\n\nIt's a modal verb like *müssen*: no ending for *ich* and *er/sie*, and the second verb goes to the end.\n\n- ich **soll**\n- du **sollst**\n- er / sie **soll**\n- wir sollen\n- ihr sollt\n- sie / Sie sollen\n\n**viel** = a lot (of), as in *Wie viel?*",
          "examples": [
            { "text": "Ich soll viel Wasser trinken.", "translation": "I'm supposed to drink a lot of water." },
            { "text": "Du sollst viel schlafen.", "translation": "You should sleep a lot." },
            { "text": "Er soll heute nicht arbeiten.", "translation": "He's not supposed to work today." }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "hl4-e2",
          "type": "MATCH_PAIRS",
          "pairs": [
            { "target": "ich soll", "base": "I should" },
